# Artifact Registry garbage collection

The free Artifact Registry allowance is **0.5 GB for the whole billing account**, then about $0.10 per GB per month. Old untagged images from earlier deploys are what crosses that line.

After every deploy that pushes a container (Cloud Run, Cloud Build, `gcloud run jobs deploy --source`, `gcloud builds submit`):

1. Run `scripts/gc_artifact_registry.sh` from this repo. It covers every project on the same billing account, not only the project just deployed.
2. The script deletes untagged images whose digest is not still referenced by a Cloud Run job or service. It keeps `latest` and any digest a live revision pins.
3. Each Docker repository must have a cleanup policy that deletes untagged images older than 1 day. The script sets that policy if it is missing. Leave vulnerability scanning disabled.

Do not deploy a second copy of an image "just in case." One tag per app. Do not enable `containerscanning.googleapis.com`.
